<center><h1 style="padding:0px 5px 0px 5px; font-family:garamond;">APA (American Psychological Association)</h1></center>

<p style="padding:0px 5px 0px 5px;font-size:20px;font-family:garamond;"><a style="color:#060; text-decoration:none;" href="http://www.apa.org">The American Psychological Association</a> (APA) publishes a writing and documentation style manual emphasizing highly structured textual progression, thorough citations, and textual methods for preventing bias.<a style="color:#060; text-decoration:none;" href="http://www.apastyle.org"> APA Style</a> rigidly partitions works into prescribed sections: title, abstract, introduction, method, results, discussion, references, and appendices. Dividing every paper into these same sections allows readers familiar with APA style to quickly locate the information they seek. APA style’s methods are especially suited for publishing scientific research and surveys of scientific research in the social and behavioral sciences. Like MLA style, APA style uses parenthetical citations directing readers to an alphabetical list of  “References” near the end of the paper to complete documentation.</p>


<p style="padding:0px 5px 0px 5px;font-size:20px;font-family:garamond;">The Southeastern Louisiana University Writing center has an <a style="color:#060; text-decoration:none;" href="http://www.southeastern.edu/acad_research/programs/writing_center/handouts/pdf_handouts/apaupdated2010.pdf">APA Style Guide</a> and a thorough <a style="color:#060; text-decoration:none;" href="http://www.southeastern.edu/acad_research/programs/writing_center/handouts/pdf_handouts/apastylechecklist.pdf">APA Style Checklist</a> on its website. Perdue University’s Online Writing Lab (OWL) maintains extensive <a style="color:#060; text-decoration:none;" href="https://owl.english.purdue.edu/owl/section/2/10/">explanations and examples</a> of APA style on its website. The APA has a free Basics of APA Style tutorial on its website.</p>


